IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wca-core`

-- Workers Compensation Act 1951 (ACT) -- from the seat of the insurer.
--
-- SEAT: the insurer of the claim (s 127(1)): the licensed insurer with the employer's compulsory insurance policy, or
-- the employer itself as a licensed self-insurer. A licensed insurer is a private party, not an official, and the Act
-- gives it hard deadlines with consequences: 72 hours to flag a deficient medical certificate (s 119), 28 days before it
-- is taken to accept (s 128), 2 or 8 weeks of further weekly compensation after a rejection (ss 130-131), the court's
-- leave after a year (s 132), and the liability to pay until it rejects or settles (s 134). "Is the claim taken to
-- comply? Am I taken to have accepted it? When may I stop paying? Can I get any of it back?" The rules are in
-- wca-core.l4; this module restates none, and keeps its own names (none shared with wca-seat.l4 or
-- wca-seat-employer.l4). The DI fund (the default insurance fund) is out of scope.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Compensation Act 1951 (ACT) -- the insurer's questions`

§§ `The medical certificate (s 116(2), s 118(2), s 119)`

@export Is this claim for weekly compensation taken to comply with the medical certificate requirement (s 118(2), s 119)?
GIVEN `the claim is for weekly compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for weekly compensation (which must come with a medical certificate, s 116(2))
      `the certificate meets s 118(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the certificate meets the prescribed requirements and states the doctor's assessment of whether the condition is consistent with employment being a substantial contributing factor
      `I told the worker in writing within 72 hours what was missing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you told the worker in writing, with details of what is required, within 72 hours after receiving the claim
      `I waived the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you waived the requirement for the claim to comply with s 118(2)
GIVETH A `Certificate answer`
DECIDE `Is the claim taken to comply with the certificate requirement` IS
    `the medical certificate position` `the claim is for weekly compensation` `the certificate meets s 118(2)` `I told the worker in writing within 72 hours what was missing` `I waived the requirement`

@export Within how many hours of receiving a claim must I flag a deficient medical certificate, or the claim is taken to comply (s 119(2)-(3))?
GIVEN `I am asking about a claim for weekly compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for weekly compensation
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many hours must I flag a deficient certificate` IS
    IF `I am asking about a claim for weekly compensation` THEN `the hours to flag a deficient medical certificate` ELSE 0

§§ `Accepting or rejecting the claim (pt 6.2, s 134)`

@export Am I taken to have accepted the claim because I did not decide to reject it within 28 days (s 128)?
GIVEN `the claim is for an imminently fatal asbestos-related disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for an imminently fatal asbestos-related disease (s 128A; not covered here)
      `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the claim (ISO date)
      `I decided to reject the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have decided to reject the claim
      `the day I decided to reject it` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you decided (otherwise any date)
GIVETH AN `Acceptance answer`
DECIDE `Am I taken to have accepted the claim` IS
    `whether the claim is taken to be accepted` `the claim is for an imminently fatal asbestos-related disease` `the day I received the claim` `I decided to reject the claim` `the day I decided to reject it`

-- Situation: the insurer has rejected, or means to reject, the claim.
@export I have rejected the claim: from what day may I stop paying weekly compensation (ss 129-132, s 134)?
GIVEN `the day the claim was given to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was given to you, or you were given notice of it by the employer or the worker (s 127(2))
      `the day the last of the worker and the employer received my rejection notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the rejection notice was received by the worker and (unless you are a self-insurer) the employer, whichever was later (s 129(2)-(3))
      `my notice gives the reason, and if late a statement explaining why` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your notice gives the reason (not just "medical reasons") and, if given 28 days or more after the claim, a statement explaining why (s 129(4)-(6))
      `my only ground is that I have not had time to assess the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your only ground for rejecting is that you have not had time to assess the claim adequately (s 130(2))
      `the Magistrates Court gave me leave to reject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Magistrates Court gave you leave to reject (needed from 1 year after the claim was given, s 132)
      `the order states a day to stop payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court's order states a day on which you may stop paying
      `the day the court's order states` IS A DATE @desc That day, if stated (otherwise any date)
      `the day the worker was given notice of my rejection` IS A DATE @desc For a rejection with leave: the day of the leave if the worker or the worker's lawyer was there, otherwise the day the worker received your notice (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A `Stop answer`
DECIDE `From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` IS
    `when weekly compensation may stop after a rejection`
        (`Rejection facts` WITH
            `the day the claim was given to the insurer`                               IS `the day the claim was given to me`
            `the day the claim is taken to be rejected`                                IS `the day the last of the worker and the employer received my rejection notice`
            `the notice gives the reason, and from 28 days a statement explaining why` IS `my notice gives the reason, and if late a statement explaining why`
            `the only ground is that the insurer has not had time to assess the claim` IS `my only ground is that I have not had time to assess the claim`
            `the Magistrates Court gave leave to reject`                               IS `the Magistrates Court gave me leave to reject`
            `the court's order states a day to stop`                                   IS `the order states a day to stop payments`
            `the day stated in the order`                                              IS `the day the court's order states`
            `the day the worker got notice of the rejection`                           IS `the day the worker was given notice of my rejection`)

@export May I recover the weekly compensation I paid on the claim, from the worker or the employer (s 128(2)(b), s 134(2)-(4))?
GIVEN `the employer gave me the injury notice more than 48 hours after becoming aware of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer gave you the injury notice late, so that s 95 makes the employer liable for weekly compensation until the notice
      `I am the employer, as a licensed self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the employer itself, holding a self-insurer licence
GIVETH A `Recovery answer`
DECIDE `May I recover what I paid on the claim` IS
    `what the insurer may recover` `the employer gave me the injury notice more than 48 hours after becoming aware of the injury` `I am the employer, as a licensed self-insurer`
